# Mutant 37 — R-UI-7
# Description: "Total clicks: N" and "Clicks in range: N" are rendered with thousands separators
#   (`1,234`), so N is no longer a plain base-10 integer once a link has 1,000 or more clicks. Links with
#   fewer clicks render identically; the per-day and breakdown tables are unchanged.
# Why realistic: formatting a big number for humans is a reflexive "polish" change.
# Trigger (gray-box): seed >= 1000 clicks for a link (or run the R-REDIR-5 load test twice on one link);
#   GET /links/{code} -> the text reads "Total clicks: 1,000".

